  "reference_notes": "Compared broad leathery alternate foliage and spreading evergreen woodland colonies to revised current pilots 1/4/7 and the full 36 sheet. The first tight upright hedge-like pilot was rejected during research. Reduced stems to three-to-five, secondary forks to one and leaf positions to four; widened spread and rounded blade envelopes while retaining attached stems. The revised crowns have separate outward shoots and openings rather than a clipped ball. Height approximately 0.70-1.48 m. Selected vegetative spring foliage before the small pendent flower racemes; no berries. Fine leaf serration and sheen are unresolved/current-palette limitations. Accepted as a stylized salal colony unit.",
